BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 522.00 Tm (Overview) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 490.00 Tm (This repository is an Express and MongoDB backend for a small e-commerce product management API.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 476.00 Tm (It includes user authentication, JWT-based protected routes, product CRUD APIs, ImageKit image) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 462.00 Tm (uploads, and MongoDB persistence through Mongoose.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 440.00 Tm (The original code had a working beginner-level structure, but several important boundaries were) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.00 Tm (mixed together. Controllers, services, validation, environment configuration, database access,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.00 Tm (and upload handling were not cleanly separated. The review focused on keeping the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 398.00 Tm (application idea while making the code safer, easier to maintain, and closer to production-style) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 384.00 Tm (backend practices.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 354.00 Tm (Issues Found) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 322.00 Tm (1. Product service used `res.status\(...\).json\(...\)` even though `res` is not available inside the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 308.00 Tm (service layer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 294.00 Tm (2. Product ownership was broken because products were stored with email, while queries tried to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 280.00 Tm (filter using a non-existing `id` field.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 266.00 Tm (3. Product read, update, and delete operations did not verify that the product belonged to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 252.00 Tm (logged-in user.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 238.00 Tm (4. Product upload logic imported ImageKit incorrectly after the config changed, which could break) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 224.00 Tm (create/update flows at runtime.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 210.00 Tm (5. Product service called `files.map\(...\)` directly, so requests without files could crash.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 196.00 Tm (6. Product validation was mostly inside the service layer instead of request middleware.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 182.00 Tm (7. File uploads had no file type or file size protection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 168.00 Tm (8. Auth responses could expose user documents too directly, including sensitive fields in earlier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 154.00 Tm (flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 140.00 Tm (9. Password selection and comparison were not fully hardened in the model/service boundary.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 126.00 Tm (10. JWT verification used raw environment access and did not return a clean 401 for malformed or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 112.00 Tm (expired tokens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 98.00 Tm (11. Auth middleware only handled cookie tokens, while API documentation also referenced Bearer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 84.00 Tm (tokens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.00 70.00 Tm (12. Environment variables were not documented with an example file.) Tj ET
endstream
